MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m01_001: This Obelisk Chamber is a special room that I spent\na long time preparing.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m01_002: 'Tis cut off from the flow of time in the world of the\nliving. The room itself functions as a sort of barrier.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m01_003: And so none but I can reach it from the outside.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m01_004: That is why, even within Dagsion, we are safe so\nlong as we are here.
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Fot_m01: <BLN>We are safe here.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot__m02_001: To bring those who have already died forward into\nthis future is a bit tricky.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_002: It involves bending the law of cause and effect,\nsubtly changing the original conclusion.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_003: Because of our particular interferences, the resulting\nevents each time are a bit different.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_004: But 'tis not a case of diverging roads. All the futures\nwe shape lead here.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_005: If I had to explain... 'Tis like multiple laws of cause\nand effect combined into a composite.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_006: The many established pasts are layered on top of\none another, but all are part of the same whole.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_007: 'Tis conceivable that these contradictory memories\nmay give rise to some confusion.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_008: A person may meet someone they remembered to be\ndead, carrying an object that was never created.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02_009: But these small eddies in the flow of time are far\npreferable to the current state of the world.
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Fot_m02: <BLN>'Tis a long explanation, but...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m03_001: I'm sure you have questions regarding the\nmechanisms of causality.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m03_002: But they can all be answered by saying that what you\nwitness beyond these obelisks is considered truth.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m03_003: Just know that our windows of interference with\neach person's causality are limited.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m03_004: We must carefully choose our moments to tip the\nscales in our favor.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Fot_m03_005: And when I say "we," I mean "I."
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Fot_m03: <BLN>In essence...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m01_001: I didn't think there was room in blighted Dagsion for\na chamber like this.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m01_002: A strange space. It's so pure...and quiet.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m01_003: As if time in here is separate from the world outside.
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Kou_m01: <BLN>This is a strange space...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m02_001: Can we really mount an opposition to Balor?
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m02_002: Sorry. I nearly lost my nerve for a moment there.
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Kou_m02: <BLN>I can't help but be anxious...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m03_001: No doubt Nuwa has stopped functioning entirely\nby now.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m03_002: I've only read what remains in the village records\nand heard a bit more from Master Zenon, but...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m03_003: apparently that ship's name comes from the snake in\nan ancient, long-forgotten creation myth.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m03_004: The old world had a number of ships the size of\nNuwa, or so they say.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Kou_m03_005: The thought of it boggles the mind...
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Kou_m03: <BLN>The scale is overwhelming.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m01_001: I've been thinking about what Fortuna said.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m01_002: If she's right, multiple observed results will be fused\ntogether, one on top of the next.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m01_003: It's hard to reconcile the law of causality here with\nthe uncertainty principle.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m01_004: But who knows? This is far from the world I thought\nI knew all those years ago. I can't keep up anymore.
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Tro_m01: <BLN>Frankly...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m02_001: It was a desperate measure for Zenon to give you his\nown Heart Core. Such a thing is almost unheard of.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m02_002: He gave you everything he could, in a very literal\nsense. Make sure his final gift isn't wasted.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m02_003: This will be humanity's world, or it will be Balor's,\nand which it is will fall to you.
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Tro_m02: <BLN>A desperate measure...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m03_001: By the way...the culture vat, or incubation tank...\nhow did you find it? Was it comfortable?
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m03_002: It just occurred to me how boring it must have been\nif you were conscious before your body was finished.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m03_003: I was made in a tank like yours too, you know.\nThough that was a long time ago.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m03_004: So don't go thinking I'm some random elder. I may\nbe getting on in years, but this body is custom-built.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c03_Tro_m03_005: Nuwa was getting old too... Yours must have been\na difficult birth, but I'm sure she's proud.
MID_LGA_0XXX_c03_Tro_m03: <BLN>She did good work.